commit 81bf153c9c84c79e87485772fd89891c4f445d4c
Author: Bart Van Assche <bvanassche@acm.org>
Date:   Sun Sep 24 15:16:11 2023 -0700

    apps: Use netsnmp_cleanup_session()
    
    The changes compared to an earlier attempt (commit 21b16eba6024 ("apps: Use
    netsnmp_cleanup_session()")) are as follows:
    - netsnmp_cleanup_session() is now called for all session objects allocated
      on the stack instead of only for a subset of these objects.
    - A copy of strings is assigned to netsnmp_session members.
    - If an snmp_close() call is followed by a netsnmp_cleanup_session() call,
      the netsnmp_session object is cleared to prevent a double free.
    
    This patch should not reintroduce
    https://github.com/net-snmp/net-snmp/issues/707.

